        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Harun al-Rashid</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 763 CE – 809 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">Between 763 and 766 (17 March 763 and February 766 are the most probable dates), at Rey in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jibal">Jibal</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>; son of the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdi">Mahdi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-khayzuran">al-Khayzuran</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">24 March 809, of an illness, at Sanabad village in Tus, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorasan">Khorasan</a>, while marching against the rebel Rafi ibn al-Layth; buried there in the Dar al-Imarah</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">Nominal leader of campaigns against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a>, 780 and 782; crown prince and governor of the empire's western territories, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>; fifth Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>, September 786 – March 809</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">A reign traditionally seen as the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islamic-golden-age">Islamic Golden Age</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-wisdom">Bayt al-Hikma</a> (&quot;House of Wisdom&quot;) in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>; campaigns against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a>; the exchange of embassies and gifts with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>; the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barmakids">Barmakids</a>; his place in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/one-thousand-and-one-nights">One Thousand and One Nights</a></span></div>
